<span id="vtabs-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="vtabs-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="vtabs-behavior-title"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">how it works</p><h2 id="vtabs-behavior-title">
      One switch. No reload. No second address bar.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Switch layouts instantly.</h3><p>
        Choose View → Tab Layout → Vertical Tabs, or press Command or Control
        Alt V. The page you are reading stays exactly where it is — nothing
        reloads.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A rail that fits your session.</h3><p>
        Every open tab becomes a row with its title, so a wide session stays
        readable instead of shrinking into dots. Drag the rail's edge to the
        width you want; Blanc remembers it on this device.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Drag tabs into the order you want.</h3><p>
        Drag a tab or a group header in the rail to reorder it, move a tab
        between groups, or move a whole group. On a focused row,
        Option+Shift+Up or Down on a Mac, or Alt+Shift+Up or Down on Windows
        and Linux, does the same from the keyboard. The expanded Island uses
        the same moves.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Still one island.</h3><p>
        The rail is an overview, not a second interface. Searching, navigating,
        and commands stay on the island, so nothing you have learned about Blanc
        changes.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="vtabs-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2 id="vtabs-note-title">
    The island layout stays the default.
  </h2><p>
    Blanc starts in its island layout, and vertical tabs are a choice you make
    per device — the setting never syncs, so a rail on your desktop does not
    rearrange your laptop. Switch back the same way you switched in.
  </p><a
    class="text-link"
    href="/support#quiet-tabs"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="vertical-tabs"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >See how Quiet Tabs save memory <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</aside>
